<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Garage replacement in Calgary usually means a 1950s to 1980s single garage on a back lane that has outlived its sills, its slab or its door opening. This site puts Calgary homeowners in touch with independent garage builders. The builder who quotes your job contracts directly with you for the demolition, the new garage and the permit applications, and this site does none of that work itself.</p><p>What the new garage costs is only part of it. A replacement quote has to say what comes down, where the old slab and materials go, what happens to the power and gas lines, and which permit covers the new structure. Get two or three written quotes that list those items the same way, and start early, before the spring rush. If you would rather talk it through first, call (403) 555-0162.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Repair and rebuild priced side by side</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Ask the builder to price the repair and the full replacement on the same garage. The City lists permit fees of $205.92 for renovating an existing garage and $333.84 for a new one, so the permit is a small line and the structure drives the price.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Demolition scope in writing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">One Calgary builder's demolition scope covers removal and disposal of the pad, walls and roof structure, plus removal and capping of electrical and gas lines. Your quote should name each item the same way.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Slab assessed, not assumed</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Whether the old slab stays is the builder's call after looking at it. One Calgary builder says an existing pad needs assessment before construction, and another includes pad removal in its demolition scope.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">One permit for the new structure</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">When an old garage is demolished and replaced, the City says the demolition is included in the permit for the new structure. The new garage needs a building permit, which the City says takes approximately 7 days to review.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Today's rules, not the old footprint</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The new garage is checked against the current Land Use Bylaw: side and rear setbacks, 1.0 m from the house, a 4.6 m height limit. A garage that sat where it liked in 1965 may not be allowed to sit there now.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Utilities dealt with before the dig</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Underground lines get located before any digging, and a new garage always needs its own electrical permit. Ask who handles the disconnect, the capping and the new subpanel, and whether a Master Electrician pulls the permit.</p>
      </div>
</div>
